diff --git a/docs/HARDWARE-CPU-INTEGRATION.md b/docs/HARDWARE-CPU-INTEGRATION.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..60fd411
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/HARDWARE-CPU-INTEGRATION.md
@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@
+# Hardware CPU dependency integration
+
+This candidate starts at published LightingSimulation 83a6acf8421356473a61336b0d58a504f7b40da8. It exports HardwareCpuBoard and makes native_board_call execute the production RTL CPU through the real MainboardFPGA bridge. Missing bridge configuration is an error. SoftwareCpuBoard remains a separately named reference implementation.
+
+CPU replies have 32 fields; mainboard replies have 17. Validation and accessKind travel through CPU, Rust transport, mainboard and memory controller. Instruction/page-table requests reject MMIO before target access. Validation does not read or modify target storage.
+
+Own Git dependencies: SIA ae9d5771a788d374c7be86e77da3724252b5fd06; RealCard b09117c762a36f6d25256fc3d0de3c212ada2d61. SIA's update changes only repository metadata/Cargo.lock; registry dependencies remain unchanged. RealCard is a local tested candidate awaiting explicit feature publication authorization; this candidate cannot be fetched reproducibly from GitHub until that commit is published.
+
+## Reproduce
+
+Use the matching LightingChips integration candidate. Run its tools/build-cpu-integration-bridges.py with --bsc and --lighting pointing here, then tools/check-cpu-integration-rtl.py. Run tools/prepare-cpu-integration-inputs.py and compile tests/boot/workload.fg with Forge's forge-lighting-firmware SOURCE --raw-image --text-base 0x1000 -o IMAGE.
+
+Export PATH containing BSC/bin and BLUESPECDIR=BSC/lib. Set LIGHTING_CPU_BOARD_BRIDGE and LIGHTING_MAINBOARD_M6_MULTISLOT_BRIDGE to the freshly built bridge executables, LIGHTING_COMPILED_BOARD_WORKLOAD to IMAGE, and LIGHTING_TRANSLATED_BOARD_FIXTURES to the generated fixtures directory. Run cargo test --offline --locked --test hardware_cpu_board -- --nocapture. Reject SKIP output; all six tests must run. Ten independent encoding/assembler/software-board reference tests also passed with the new SIA pin.
+
+This proves Bluesim production RTL integration, not physical FPGA timing or board bring-up. No physical FPGA part, pin constraints or timing closure is selected here. Unrelated Cosmic M29/M30, storage, DMA-priority and QDX changes are excluded.
